REASONING=Three independent finite verbs: "sumus" (linking, with "filii" as predicate nominative, "omnes" adjectival to it, "unius viri" a genitive with "unius" adjectival to "viri"); "venimus" (intransitive, with "pacifici" as a predicate adjective describing the unexpressed subject); and "machinantur" (deponent, transitive active, with "famuli tui" as subject, "quidquam" as direct object, and "mali" as a partitive genitive depending on "quidquam"). "nec" is a coordinating conjunction joining "venimus" and "machinantur" (and carrying the negation). Punctuation tokens take no relations.

